Authentication Flow

The authentication process is managed through Keycloak’s Single Sign-On (SSO) portal using the OpenID Connect (OIDC) protocol. When a user logs in, Keycloak validates the provided credentials and issues a set of session tokens based on OAuth 2.0 standards. These include an ID token that contains user identity claims and an access token used to request access to protected resources. Both tokens are encoded as JWTs and securely transmitted to the client application for use in subsequent API interactions.

