Authorization Flow

Once authentication is complete, the issued access token is attached to each API request sent to the Validium and Paladin backend services. These services validate the token’s signature and claims through Keycloak’s JWKS endpoint to ensure its authenticity and integrity. Authorization decisions are then enforced based on the token’s embedded roles, scopes, and organizational claims (such as org_id or bic). This centralized model ensures consistent, role-based access control and secure interaction between all components within the shared environment.